**Case 2:** Suppose $C$ is false (i.e., colorectal cancer is not a bile duct cancer).

If $C$ is false, then $\neg C$ is true. Therefore, the statement $M \lor \neg C$ becomes $M \lor T$, which is true regardless of whether $M$ is true or false.

