Since we have deduced that $\neg N(T)$ (Taylor does not fulfill her nutritional daily intakes), and from the contrapositive of $P(x) \implies N(x)$, which is $\neg N(x) \implies \neg P(x)$, this is consistent with $\neg P(T)$ (since $\neg N(T)$ implies $\neg P(T)$, and we already know $\neg P(T)$).

