Now, going back to statement 2, $P \lor I$. Since we have established that $\neg I$ (Bonnie is not inactive and disinterested), the only way for $P \lor I$ to be true is if $P$ is true. Therefore, if Bonnie both attends and is very engaged with school events and is a student who attends the school, then she must perform in school talent shows often ($P$).

